1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:04,715
Every team agreed to a fourteen-day trial.

2
00:00:05,271 --> 00:00:08,408
Product meant fourteen days after the customer's first use.

3
00:00:09,009 --> 00:00:12,525
Billing meant fourteen days after email verification.

4
00:00:13,202 --> 00:00:15,740
The same word, activated, hid a different event.

5
00:00:16,262 --> 00:00:21,303
A customer who starts using the product
a week later is charged seven days early.

6
00:00:21,872 --> 00:00:25,588
PARALLAX finds this false agreement before the customer does.

7
00:00:25,900 --> 00:00:30,416
It connects what teams promise, what systems do, and the people

8
00:00:30,416 --> 00:00:31,907
responsible for the handoff.

9
00:00:33,220 --> 00:00:35,834
FalkorDB is the operational core.

10
00:00:36,569 --> 00:00:40,218
Sources connect to reviewed interpretations, executable rules,

11
00:00:40,630 --> 00:00:42,944
shared obligations, events, and owners.

12
00:00:43,455 --> 00:00:48,729
Agents discover tools through MCP, follow multiple graph hops, run a

13
00:00:48,729 --> 00:00:53,079
bounded counterexample check, and save
evidence and actions back into the graph.

14
00:00:54,234 --> 00:00:57,125
Here is the workspace, with six handoff scenarios.

15
00:00:58,160 --> 00:01:00,052
Let's investigate the trial handoff.

16
00:01:01,098 --> 00:01:04,669
The investigator traces Product's promise through Engineering's event

17
00:01:04,669 --> 00:01:06,370
contract to Billing's scheduler.

18
00:01:07,071 --> 00:01:11,222
The verifier checks both rules against the same customer timeline.

19
00:01:12,535 --> 00:01:17,363
The result is concrete: email verified on day zero, first use on day

20
00:01:17,363 --> 00:01:21,968
seven, a charge on day fourteen, but promised access until day twenty-one.

21
00:01:22,781 --> 00:01:27,731
Each result includes its input bounds,
source versions, and evaluation trace.

22
00:01:28,266 --> 00:01:30,636
Different wording alone never proves a conflict.

23
00:01:31,350 --> 00:01:36,345
The coordinator opens one clarification
case and finds accountable owners using

24
00:01:36,345 --> 00:01:39,071
FalkorDB's shortest-path algorithm.

25
00:01:39,683 --> 00:01:41,741
A person chooses the intended meaning.

26
00:01:42,208 --> 00:01:46,080
Approval records the decision and creates implementation tasks.

27
00:01:46,492 --> 00:01:47,638
The case stays open.

28
00:01:48,511 --> 00:01:52,182
For this synthetic demo, we now record evidence for the event,

29
00:01:52,360 --> 00:01:54,519
billing, and quality-assurance tasks.

30
00:01:55,264 --> 00:01:59,369
Only after every task is complete can PARALLAX run a fresh check

31
00:01:59,447 --> 00:02:01,094
over the full declared domain.

32
00:02:02,017 --> 00:02:05,110
The adopted mapping passes, and the case resolves.

33
00:02:05,867 --> 00:02:08,537
The original counterexample remains in history.

34
00:02:09,525 --> 00:02:11,504
Memory survives the conversation.

35
00:02:11,972 --> 00:02:13,952
Episodic memory records what happened.

36
00:02:14,519 --> 00:02:17,022
Semantic memory preserves reviewed meaning.

37
00:02:17,489 --> 00:02:21,094
Procedural memory records how the team handles this kind of handoff.

38
00:02:21,596 --> 00:02:25,143
Every agent can recall relevant memory, while revision checks

39
00:02:25,143 --> 00:02:27,135
reject outdated conclusions.

40
00:02:28,813 --> 00:02:32,061
Separate tenant graphs keep the two demo companies apart.

41
00:02:32,651 --> 00:02:37,513
The verification lab measures concurrent
reads and writes, revision conflicts,

42
00:02:37,702 --> 00:02:40,160
idempotency, and agent ownership.

43
00:02:40,861 --> 00:02:45,590
These are measured checks against FalkorDB, with results you can inspect.

44
00:02:46,641 --> 00:02:51,125
PARALLAX brings both Graph Hacks tracks together: agents that act

45
00:02:51,125 --> 00:02:55,041
on connected evidence, and agents that remember and coordinate.

46
00:02:55,564 --> 00:02:58,000
Shared words deserve shared meaning.
